| recvldbETaKfTG | Auth schema, user struct, and accounts context | ["Open"] | ["P1"] | recvld7oDU6zzL |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | This is a sub-task of a larger decomposition.<br><br>Create the foundation for user authentication. This sub-task creates three files: (1) `lib/symphony_elixir/auth/user.ex` — an Ecto embedded schema (`SymphonyElixir.Auth.User`) with fields `id` (autogenerate UUID), `email` (unique, validated), `password_hash`, `inserted_at`, `updated_at`. Include an Ecto changeset for registration (validates email format, password length ≥8) and one for login (validates email+password against hash). Use `Bcrypt` for password hashing via `Bcrypt.hash_pwd_salt/1` and `Bcrypt.verify_pass/2`. (2) `lib/symphony_elixir/auth/accounts.ex` — `SymphonyElixir.Auth.Accounts` context module with functions `register_user/1` (accepts attrs map, returns `{:ok, %User{}}` or `{:error, changeset}`), `authenticate_user/2` (accepts email + password, returns `{:ok, %User{}}` or `{:error, :unauthorized}`), `get_user/1` (lookup by id). Store users in an ETS table (`SymphonyElixir.Auth.UserStore`) created via a `GenServer` at startup — no external DB needed. (3) `lib/symphony_elixir/auth/user_store.ex` — `SymphonyElixir.Auth.UserStore` GenServer that manages the ETS table with `insert/1`, `lookup/1`, `lookup_by_email/1`, `delete/1`. Add this GenServer to the application supervision tree in the existing `lib/symphony_elixir/application.ex`. Add `{:bcrypt_elixir, "~> 3.2"}` to deps in `mix.exs`.<br><br>Scope: New files: lib/symphony_elixir/auth/user.ex, lib/symphony_elixir/auth/accounts.ex, lib/symphony_elixir/auth/user_store.ex. Modified: mix.exs (add bcrypt_elixir dep), lib/symphony_elixir/application.ex (add UserStore to supervision tree) |  |  | ["feature"] |
| recvldbFfLO7jw | Auth plug pipeline, session helpers, and all router changes | ["Open"] | ["P1"] | recvld7oDU6zzL |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | This is a sub-task of a larger decomposition.<br><br>Create the authentication plug layer AND make all router modifications in a single sub-task to avoid file conflicts. Create two files: (1) `lib/symphony_elixir_web/plugs/auth.ex` — `SymphonyElixirWeb.Plugs.Auth` plug module with two plugs: `require_auth/2` (reads `user_id` from session, looks up user via `SymphonyElixir.Auth.Accounts.get_user/1`, assigns `@current_user` in conn or halts with 401 redirect to login path), and `redirect_if_authenticated/2` (redirects already-logged-in users away from login/register pages). (2) `lib/symphony_elixir_web/plugs/current_user.ex` — `SymphonyElixirWeb.Plugs.CurrentUser` plug that runs on every browser request (non-blocking): if session has `user_id`, fetch user and assign `@current_user`; if not, set `@current_user` to `nil`. This plug goes in the `:browser` pipeline AFTER `fetch_session`. (3) Update `lib/symphony_elixir_web/router.ex` — ALL changes in one place: add `plug(SymphonyElixirWeb.Plugs.CurrentUser)` to the existing `:browser` pipeline, create a new `:authenticated` pipeline that pipes through `:browser` and adds `plug(SymphonyElixirWeb.Plugs.Auth, require_auth: true)`, add login/logout routes under a public scope: `get "/login", SessionController, :new`, `post "/login", SessionController, :create`, `delete "/logout", SessionController, :delete`. Move dashboard live route under the `:authenticated` pipeline.<br><br>Scope: New files: lib/symphony_elixir_web/plugs/auth.ex, lib/symphony_elixir_web/plugs/current_user.ex. Modified: lib/symphony_elixir_web/router.ex (add plugs to pipeline, create :authenticated pipeline, add login/logout routes) |  |  | ["feature"] |
